{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U2GhkkxYQvGeFXMDo4tspP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: judge-bias-contamination-research\n3\tdescription: LLM judge bias与benchmark contamination领域的实验设计共识、竞品定位、方法论趋势——12篇论文蒸馏\n4\ttype: skill\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Benchmark 与指标共识\n8\t\n9\t- **Judge bias 研究**用 MT-Bench（4/12）+ Arena-Hard（3/12）。Contamination 研究用 GSM8K+MMLU+ARC-C+HellaSwag 四件套（3/12）。G-MFRM 需覆盖两组。**置信度 高**\n10\t- **Human reference** 是必要验证：zheng2023 用 3K expert + 3K crowd votes，UDA 用 100 条，CyclicJudge 用 panel mean 作 proxy。**置信度 高**\n11\t- **核心指标**：Inter-judge std/Var(X̄)↓（CyclicJudge,UDA）| Agreement/Pearson r with human↑（zheng2023,UDA）| Rater parameter→0（wang2025）| Detection rate/δ̂（ConStat）| Kendall τ↑（PSN-IRT）。G-MFRM 需同时报 θ-RMSE + Kendall τ + judge/contamination 指标。\n12\t\n13\t## 方法论趋势\n14\t\n15\t**上升**：(1) Psychometric models 迁移至 LLM（MFRM, 4PL IRT, DG-IRT）(2) Multi-judge panels + 统计方法处理 judge variance (3) Performance-based contamination 定义取代 information-flow（ConStat: r²=0.94）。**置信度 高**\n16\t\n17\t**消退**：Perplexity-based 污染检测易绕过（ConStat 89% vs Shi 21.7%）；单 judge 已不可接受。**置信度 中**\n18\t\n19\t## G-MFRM 竞品定位\n20\t\n21\t| 竞品 | Judge Bias | Contamination | 可解释 | G-MFRM 优势 |\n22\t|------|:-:|:-:|:-:|------|\n23\t| CyclicJudge | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | 联合建模 |\n24\t| UDA | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | 可解释+contamination |\n25\t| DCR | ✗ | ✓ | 部分 | judge facet |\n26\t| ConStat | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | judge facet |\n27\t| PSN-IRT | ✗ | 间接 | ✓ | multi-facet+judge |\n28\t\n29\t**核心空白（0/12篇）**：无论文同时建模 judge severity 与 contamination 的 confounding。CyclicJudge 证明 judge bias 占 >94% variance 但忽略 contamination；DCR 调整 accuracy 但忽略 judge。**置信度 高**\n30\t\n31\t## 实验设计经验\n32\t\n33\t- **Judge panel**：5-10 judges from ≥3 families（CyclicJudge, UDA, wang2025）**置信度 中**\n34\t- **Position swap**：pairwise evaluation 标准操作（zheng2023）**置信度 高**\n35\t- **显著性检验**：Bootstrap + BH 校正（ConStat, preference_leakage）或 paired Wilcoxon **置信度 高**\n36\t- **Self-preference**：judge 自评偏高是 universal pattern（CyclicJudge: Qwen 自评第一但共识排最后；UDA: [-21%,+56%] deviation）——G-MFRM 的 d_j 应捕获 **置信度 高**\n37\t\n38\t## 共同局限 → G-MFRM 卖点\n39\t\n40\t1. Judge bias 和 contamination 分别处理（6/12）→ joint estimation\n41\t2. 无 confounding 分析（0/12）→ ρ(d_j, c_n·e_i) 实验\n42\t3. 小规模验证（wang2025: 30人, CyclicJudge: 5 judges）→ 更大规模\n43\t4. 闭源模型训练数据不透明（4/12）→ black-box compatible\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78fb0fb0-9a26-4b0a-9a95-b4189f601ffb","uuid":"dda9b416-c415-4043-93d2-a9e19a8899d5","timestamp":"2026-05-22T04:53:28.674Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod43/skills/projects/gated_mfrm_judge_bias/distilled-research.skill.md","content":"---\nname: judge-bias-contamination-research\ndescription: LLM judge bias与benchmark contamination领域的实验设计共识、竞品定位、方法论趋势——12篇论文蒸馏\ntype: skill\n---\n\n## Benchmark 与指标共识\n\n- **Judge bias 研究**用 MT-Bench（4/12）+ Arena-Hard（3/12）。Contamination 研究用 GSM8K+MMLU+ARC-C+HellaSwag 四件套（3/12）。G-MFRM 需覆盖两组。**置信度 高**\n- **Human reference** 是必要验证：zheng2023 用 3K expert + 3K crowd votes，UDA 用 100 条，CyclicJudge 用 panel mean 作 proxy。**置信度 高**\n- **核心指标**：Inter-judge std/Var(X̄)↓（CyclicJudge,UDA）| Agreement/Pearson r with human↑（zheng2023,UDA）| Rater parameter→0（wang2025）| Detection rate/δ̂（ConStat）| Kendall τ↑（PSN-IRT）。G-MFRM 需同时报 θ-RMSE + Kendall τ + judge/contamination 指标。\n\n## 方法论趋势\n\n**上升**：(1) Psychometric models 迁移至 LLM（MFRM, 4PL IRT, DG-IRT）(2) Multi-judge panels + 统计方法处理 judge variance (3) Performance-based contamination 定义取代 information-flow（ConStat: r²=0.94）。**置信度 高**\n\n**消退**：Perplexity-based 污染检测易绕过（ConStat 89% vs Shi 21.7%）；单 judge 已不可接受。**置信度 中**\n\n## G-MFRM 竞品定位\n\n| 竞品 | Judge Bias | Contamination | 可解释 | G-MFRM 优势 |\n|------|:-:|:-:|:-:|------|\n| CyclicJudge | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | 联合建模 |\n| UDA | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | 可解释+contamination |\n| DCR | ✗ | ✓ | 部分 | judge facet |\n| ConStat | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | judge facet |\n| PSN-IRT | ✗ | 间接 | ✓ | multi-facet+judge |\n\n**核心空白（0/12篇）**：无论文同时建模 judge severity 与 contamination 的 confounding。CyclicJudge 证明 judge bias 占 >94% variance 但忽略 contamination；DCR 调整 accuracy 但忽略 judge。**置信度 高**\n\n## 实验设计经验\n\n- **Judge panel**：5-10 judges from ≥3 families（CyclicJudge, UDA, wang2025）**置信度 中**\n- **Position swap**：pairwise evaluation 标准操作（zheng2023）**置信度 高**\n- **显著性检验**：Bootstrap + BH 校正（ConStat, preference_leakage）或 paired Wilcoxon **置信度 高**\n- **Self-preference**：judge 自评偏高是 universal pattern（CyclicJudge: Qwen 自评第一但共识排最后；UDA: [-21%,+56%] deviation）——G-MFRM 的 d_j 应捕获 **置信度 高**\n\n## 共同局限 → G-MFRM 卖点\n\n1. Judge bias 和 contamination 分别处理（6/12）→ joint estimation\n2. 无 confounding 分析（0/12）→ ρ(d_j, c_n·e_i) 实验\n3. 小规模验证（wang2025: 30人, CyclicJudge: 5 judges）→ 更大规模\n4. 闭源模型训练数据不透明（4/12）→ black-box compatible\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VLRwH4ExadPMikdAZFVqBK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of:\n1. The paper content (12 pages)\n2. The experiment context (review_context.yaml with all imagined experiments)\n3. The research landscape (distilled-research.skill.md)\n\nLet me now also load the writing skill for context on paper quality expectations, then compose a comprehensive review.\n\nActually, let me proceed with the review. I have enough context. The task is to:\n1. Review the paper in simple mode (1 reviewer, comprehensive)\n2. Submit via submit_dream_review_report\n\nLet me first load the submit tool schema, then compose my review.\n\n\n---\n\nNow I'm working through the paper systematically. The core contribution is G-MFRM, a staged joint calibration framework that simultaneously estimates model ability, item difficulty, judge severity, and per-model contamination susceptibility within a single psychometric model. The paper makes three key claims: judge severity and contamination susceptibility are confounded (creating omitted variable bias), sequential correction is counterproductive when confounding exists, and the proposed method addresses this through joint estimation.\n\nThe paper is well-structured with sections covering the theoretical motivation for the confounding problem, the method formulation with three-stage estimation and identifiability proofs, comprehensive experiments including data collection and exposure estimation, and extensive ablations examining judge count effects, leave-one-out validation, and adversarial robustness.\n\nLooking at the strengths, the core insight about confounding between judge severity and contamination susceptibility is genuinely novel and well-motivated—the OVB argument is compelling.\n\nThe theoretical foundation is solid with clear formalization in Section 2, including a toy example and Monte Carlo validation across 1,000 replications that demonstrates the bias amplification from sequential correction. The experimental design is impressively comprehensive, spanning 8 judges from 5 providers, 22 target models, 3 benchmarks, and 8 baselines that cover different correction approaches, with over 200K judgments collected across the datasets.\n\nThe results are compelling—achieving a Kendall's τ of 0.87 compared to UDA's 0.82 represents a meaningful improvement that generalizes across benchmarks, and the per-model contamination estimates reveal that older-generation models like GPT-4o and Claude 3 Opus are systematically overestimated by 2-4 ranking positions. The ablation studies examining judge sensitivity, leave-one-out diagnostics, and adversarial robustness are thorough and well-executed.\n\nHowever, there are some concerns worth considering. The exposure estimation in Stage 2 uses a manually weighted composite of three sources (0.55 for performance gap, 0.25 for temporal, 0.20 for LogProber), but the paper doesn't explain how these weights were determined or validated—they seem somewhat arbitrary. More fundamentally, the entire evaluation relies on Chatbot Arena Elo as ground truth, yet Arena itself has documented biases around style preferences and verbosity, so the improvement might reflect better alignment with Arena's existing biases rather than genuine ranking accuracy.\n\nThe rank-1 contamination structure assumes each model has a single dominant contamination mode, and while the Limitations section acknowledges this, the 9.1% misfit rate for c facets suggests it's a real problem for some models that deserves deeper investigation. The staged estimation procedure also introduces potential error propagation by fixing exposure estimates from Stage 2, and while the CI under-coverage (0.91 vs 0.95) is noted, the sensitivity of main results to perturbations in these estimates isn't thoroughly explored. With only 22 target models, the statistical power analysis showing 0.86 power at Δτ = 0.05 raises questions about whether the sample size is adequate for the claims being made.\n\nThe reference variants used in the performance gap method (weighted at 0.55) were created through semantic rephrasing with spline-based difficulty correction achieving R² = 0.78, but there's no transparency about which models generated these variants or whether systematic biases were introduced if they came from GPT-5.5 or Claude. Additionally, the adversarial robustness experiment references Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) findings on fragility but doesn't include their method as a baseline comparison, which seems like a missed opportunity to validate the approach.\n\nThe paper's reliance on API-based judges (GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.7, Gemini 2.5 Pro) introduces reproducibility challenges since these models evolve over time and specific API versions aren't documented, plus the evaluation cost of roughly $820 and 95 GPU-hours may be prohibitive for others trying to replicate the work. There's also room to better articulate when G-MFRM's added complexity is actually necessary versus when simpler MFRM suffices, especially given that performance is comparable at low contamination levels.\n\nNow I'm checking how the experimental design aligns with the planned experiments—data collection, exposure estimation, model fitting on real data, baseline comparisons, contamination calibration, sensitivity analyses for judge count and exposure indicators, diagnostic checks for facet fit, and confidence interval validation all appear to be covered across the relevant sections and tables.\n\nLooking at the soundness of the work, the theoretical foundation around omitted variable bias and identifiability is rigorous, and the Monte Carlo validation provides good empirical support. The staged estimation approach and reliance on Chatbot Arena as ground truth introduce some limitations, but overall I'd assess this as solid work—around 4 out of 5 on soundness. The contribution addresses a genuine gap in understanding how contamination affects model evaluation, which is exciting, though the practical impact depends on how widely these insights get adopted. gap (0/12 prior papers address the confounding). The combination of psychometric modeling with contamination detection is novel. The practical implications (per-model contamination diagnostics, ranking corrections) are valuable. The improvement magnitude (Δτ = +0.05) is meaningful but not dramatic. I'd rate this 3.5-4/5.\n\n**Reproducibility**: 8 judges from 5 providers, API costs documented, MCMC diagnostics reported, three benchmarks. However, API models may change, specific versions not documented. Code availability not mentioned. I'd rate this 3.5/5.\n\n**Overall Assessment**: This is a solid paper with a novel and well-motivated contribution. The theoretical grounding is strong, the experiments are comprehensive, and the results are convincing. The main weaknesses are in the assumptions (rank-1 contamination, Chatbot Arena as ground truth) and the staged estimation procedure. Weighing the novelty of the confounding observation against the thoroughness of the experiments, I'm settling on a 4 (Conference) rating. The work is clearly novel—first to jointly model judge bias and contamination with a new observation about omitted variable bias—and the execution is solid with interpretable diagnostics. The staged estimation is pragmatic rather than ideal, and the sample size of 22 models is somewhat modest for the statistical claims, but for EMNLP 2026's ~21% acceptance rate, this paper has a strong chance given its clear contribution and real-world utility.\n\nNow I'll draft the review report and submit it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1632,"cache_read_input_tokens":65609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1632},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78fb0fb0-9a26-4b0a-9a95-b4189f601ffb","uuid":"91f24a74-d8f0-4f32-906e-1f30ca1c9013"}
